# ── Generated output: ignored by default, with a curated publication allowlist ──
#
# Every project-owned current artifact under output/ is disposable and
# regenerable. An old ignored output/bench_cache may remain as explicitly
# documented legacy residue, but no current code reads or writes it. The active
# call store lives in cache/, which is an input directory. So the default is still
# "ignore", and the negations below
# admit only the surfaces the template's own convention calls STABLE — the ones
# `infrastructure/core/pipeline/artifacts.py` expects a fresh clone to have,
# because the artifact manifest is committed evidence and an entry a clone
# cannot produce reads as drift.
#
# What that buys: `stage_04_validate.py` can bind its report to a real manifest.
# What it costs: these are binaries that churn on every render. Slides (~19 MB),
# and bench_raw stay ignored — they are large, they are
# not cited as evidence, and nothing validates against them. cache/ is ignored
# for the same reasons and for one more: it is machine-specific. Network-authored
# ledger entries are connected to those ignored inputs by the validated receipts
# under cache/network_claim_bindings/, never by treating the cache as tracked data.
#
# The rule in docs/output_conventions.md still holds for everything here: no
# generated artifact is ever hand-edited to make a check pass.
# `!output/` must come first: this repo's core.excludesFile is the sidecar's
# .gitignore, which excludes the output/ DIRECTORY. Git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so without re-including it here every negation below is
# never evaluated. The template's own .gitignore uses the same `!output/` then
# `output/*` pair for the same reason.
!output/
output/*
!output/data/
output/data/*
!output/data/manuscript_variables.json
!output/figures/
!output/figures/**
!output/manuscript/
!output/manuscript/**
# Exact generated typography auxiliary; its bytes are checked by the manuscript contract.
output/manuscript/article_typography.sty
!output/pdf/
output/pdf/*
!output/pdf/*_combined.pdf
!output/reports/
output/reports/*
!output/reports/artifact_manifest.json
!output/reports/connected_gum.json
!output/reports/evidence_registry.json
!output/reports/gate_audit.json
!output/reports/gate_audit_ablation.json
!output/reports/manuscript_composition.json
!output/reports/rendered_provenance.json
!output/reports/validation_report.json
!output/web/
output/web/*
!output/web/_combined_manuscript.md
# index.html is the canonical deliverable of an enabled render format, so the
# template's stable-inventory check requires a fresh clone to have it. It is
# half a megabyte of diffable text from the same directory as the file above,
# unlike the slide decks, which are ~19 MB of binaries nothing cites.
!output/web/index.html
# Vendored corpora — excluded from git, checksums tracked in docs/provenance/sources.md
vendor/brown.zip
vendor/cmudict.dict
vendor/en_ewt-ud-dev.conllu
vendor/cmu_arctic/
# Staged UD Czech-PDTC shards (~90 MB, CC BY-NC-SA): the derived
# ud_czech_case_counts.json is the committed surface (decision 77)
vendor/staging_ud_czech/
# Refs are cloned external repos, not committed here
refs/
# IDE
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# The claims ledger single-writer lock is runtime state, never an artifact.
data/.claims-recorder.lock

# Memoized external-model calls. An INPUT, not an output: warming it needs a
# live Ollama server and some hours, and the release profile's coverage floor
# depends on it. See scripts/verify_release.py and docs/output_conventions.md.
cache/
adapters/
scratchpad/
/HERDR.md
/.claude/

# Local tool state — Groma and Backlog.md are optional local tooling, inert
# when their CLIs are not installed (see AGENTS.md).
.groma/
backlog/

# graft's local graph cache — regenerable, not committed (run `graft build`).
/graft/

# The per-machine declaration of the docxology/template checkout used to
# render (see docs/reference/configuration.md): a machine property, never a
# project input.
/.template-root
